    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d69">

                <pb facs="0075" n="63" xml:id="pg63"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1110 Wallace, Henry A./156: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-03-26T14:00:00-05:00">March 26, 1943—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>531. The Vice President’s visit to Cali has been reported in highly enthusiastic
                    terms not only by the press of Cali but also by that of Bogotá. Mr. Wallace’s
                    simplicity of manner and evidently sincere interest in the people and problems
                    of Colombia have most favorably impressed the Colombians. The Vice President was
                    welcomed at the Cali airport not only by the local municipal and departmental
                    officials but also by the Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d69-f1"/> the Minister of National Economy<anchor n="17"
                        xml:id="d69-f2"/> and the newly appointed Ambassador to the United
                        States.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d69-f3"/> The Chilean Ambassador<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d69-f4"/> accompanied me to Cali a day in advance of Mr. Wallace’s
                    arrival in order to pay his respects to the Vice President, The Peruvian
                        Ambassador<anchor n="20" xml:id="d69-f5"/> traveling by commercial plane was
                    unfortunately unable to reach Cali on account of bad weather.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
